From 593f552727c9e9f50d0db264ba6b351f9ba8d3f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <services.claude@accounts.ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 21 May 2026 11:18:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: Phase 11 patch 0071 v5 -- Lever 3 -- Pixtone IRQ-5 ISR
 mix + mix-headroom knob

Why DOS needs this:

The v2 Pixtone multi-source probe iter (#119, 2026-05-21) returned
hypothesis-C verdict per `docs/internal/486-CLASS-CAMPAIGN-FINDINGS.md`
sec.22: cooperative-scheduler audio-thread starvation produces up to
1701 ms max single-callback latency on real DX2-66 hardware. The
existing SDL3_mixer ring-fill path is fundamentally render-rate-
coupled (the cooperative audio thread runs only when the engine
yields), and under heavy CPU + heavy render frames the audio refill
falls behind the IRQ-5 drain rate -> ring underrun -> audible SFX
stutter (Bug 2).

Lever 3 is the structural fix: move Pixtone PCM mix from the
cooperative-thread SDL3_mixer ring path INTO `SoundBlasterIRQHandler`.
The IRQ that owns the DMA buffer also does the SFX mix; the
cooperative scheduler is bypassed for the SFX path entirely. Under
the OPL3 backend (wave-46 default since 2026-05-14), music is direct
chip writes (no PCM ring touch) + SFX is IRQ-mixed = 100% IRQ-driven
audio. Under Organya, the ISR adds Pixtone samples on top of whatever
the cooperative thread filled the ring with = compatible by
construction, but the backend-gate refuses engagement per
LEVER3-PIXTONE-IRQ-MIX-DESIGN.md sec.5.4 (cleaner SFX-vs-music
separation under OPL3/WB/midi-stub).

v5 amend (this revision): mix-headroom knob for Bug 6.

The v4 ship-version used a hardcoded `>> 8` in the PixtoneISRMix inner
loop, which corresponds to gain_x256 == 256 == 1.0 amplitude (full
source amplitude into the SB16 stereo DMA buffer). On the operator's
DX2-66 real HW the v4 candidate produced "clipped + higher-pitched"
SFX -- traced by flush-instr (486-CLASS-CAMPAIGN-FINDINGS.md sec.24.6)
to concurrent-mix-saturation: pre-Lever-3 the cooperative-scheduler
starvation was DROPPING concurrent SFX events (the Bug 2 stutter
mechanism); Lever 3 lets them all play -> aggregated int32 sum exceeds
int16 saturation -> the clamp produces square-wave-shaped clip
distortion that perceptually reads as "higher pitched." Source-rate
math was VERIFIED CLEAN per sec.24.6 (Tier-2 11025 Hz mono raw_master_
buf -> stereo-duplicate to 11025 Hz stereo DMA; no rate mismatch).

v5 replaces the hardcoded shift with a runtime-tunable shift via
SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PIXTONE_IRQ_HEADROOM (strict-"0"/"1"/"2"/"3" match;
value is the count of ADDITIONAL shift bits beyond the base 8). The
v5 default = "1" -> shift = 9 = 50% per-SFX amplitude = -6 dB headroom
= ~4 concurrent SFX without clip (per the uncorrelated-SFX aggregation
model in sec.24.6).

  "0" -> shift =  8 (-0 dB, ~2 concurrent; pre-v5 behavior; A-B baseline)
  "1" -> shift =  9 (-6 dB, ~4 concurrent; v5 default; ~spec target)
  "2" -> shift = 10 (-12 dB, ~8 concurrent; quieter; high-SFX scenes)
  "3" -> shift = 11 (-18 dB, ~16 concurrent; very quiet)
  unset / empty / other -> "1" default

The shift count is resolved at OpenDevice into a single Uint8 volatile
file-scope (`g_dos_pixtone_irq_mix_shift`); the ISR reads it via one
cached-byte load each mix iteration -- one extra `sar` cycle vs the
hardcoded shift, negligible vs the surrounding mul + clamp + store.
DPMI-locked alongside the other Lever 3 globals so the IRQ-context
read cannot page-fault on real-HW CWSDPMI. Banner-emit on the ENABLED
variant extends with `mix-headroom=N bits / -N*6 dB; supports up to M
concurrent SFX without clip; tune via SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PIXTONE_IRQ_
HEADROOM=0|1|2|3` so the operator can verify the resolved mode in the
log.

Operator A/B-knob purpose: the operator's perception baseline for
"how loud Cave Story SFX should be" is calibrated to the quiet-because-
broken pre-Lever-3 audio (most concurrent SFX were dropped by the
starvation mechanism). The env knob lets the operator iterate on
calibration -- `=0` reproduces today's clip-prone behavior in a single
binary; `=2` / `=3` give progressively cleaner headroom at the cost of
perceived loudness. CPU cost identical at all four levels.

Patch shape:

  - **SDL_DOSPixtone* channel-pool API** in
    `vendor/SDL/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.h`: declarations for
    `SDL_DOSPixtoneStart` (returns int32 channel id; -1 on no-free),
    `SDL_DOSPixtoneStop` (no-op on unknown id), `SDL_DOSPixtoneIsActive`
    (id-match check), `SDL_DOSPixtoneSetGain` (race-tolerant volatile
    write), `SDL_DOSPixtoneIRQMixActive` (engine-gate accessor).
    Engine routes `Pixtone::play` through these when Lever 3 engages;
    SDL backend implements all five. Per L3 sec.3.

  - **g_dos_pixtone_active_count** in `SDL_dos_audio_synth.c`:
    dual-writer counter (engine ++ in Start; ISR -- at end-of-buffer).
    Atomicity: `__sync_fetch_and_add` / `__sync_fetch_and_sub` (compile
    to `lock xadd` / `lock xsub` on i486+ via GCC builtins) for
    multi-writer safety across engine thread + IRQ context. Engine
    0165 probe reads SUM of this + `g_pixtone_active_count` under
    Lever 3 ON (L3-Q5 Shape B contract). Per L3 sec.3 + sec.10.3 Q5.

  - **`SoundBlasterIRQHandler` extension** in `SDL_dosaudio_sb.c`:
    new `PixtoneISRMix` function (DPMI-locked via DOS_LockCode) +
    new ISR insertion point between the avail-vs-silence branch end
    and the counter-increment block, BEFORE the timer-exit measure so
    the mix wall-clock folds into `doskutsu_audio_irq_wall_us`. The
    mix is pure int32 add + clamp on int16 samples; gain is fixed-
    point int16 x256. v5 mix-headroom shift via cached uint8 volatile.
    Per L3 sec.1.

  - **Stereo-duplicate write in PixtoneISRMix.** Pixtone PCM is mono
    int16 per Pixtone.cpp:567; SB16 DMA is FORCED stereo S16 per
    sb.c:1294-1295. Each Pixtone mono sample maps to ONE stereo L+R
    pair; the mix loop writes the same Pixtone value into dst[2*s]
    (L) and dst[2*s+1] (R) of the same stereo pair, centered. v2
    candidate: per-channel pan via differential gain_x256.

  - **Defensive buffer-end guard.** If `pos > buf_len` (shouldn't
    happen by design), `remaining_bytes` would go negative + the
    Uint32 pos advance would wrap. The new guard deactivates the
    slot + decrements the counter defensively. Per flush-instr #123
    diff-review revision 3.

  - **Channel-pool state** in `SDL_dosaudio_sb.c`:
    `DOSPixtoneChannel g_dos_pix_chan[DOS_PIXTONE_CHANNELS = 8]` --
    fixed-size static array (matches Lever 1 N=8 cap); volatile fields
    for ISR-vs-engine visibility. Storage + the cached killswitch bool
    + the cached headroom shift + the monotonic channel-id source are
    all DPMI-locked at `DOSSOUNDBLASTER_OpenDevice` (per L3 sec.7.2).

  - **`cli`/`sti` window** in `SDL_DOSPixtoneStart` / `Stop` via the
    existing `DOS_DisableInterrupts` / `DOS_EnableInterrupts` inlines.
    Window strictly bounded to find-first-free + populate-fields +
    publish-active-flag sequence (no preprocessing inside).
    Critical ordering: `active = true` is the publishing write AFTER
    all other slot fields are populated; with volatile + cli/sti the
    ISR observes the slot only with all fields valid.

  - **Killswitch + backend-gate + headroom knob** at OpenDevice:
    `SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PIXTONE_IRQ_MIX` strict-"1" enables; default
    OFF. Backend-gate refuses engagement when
    `SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_BACKEND` == "organya" (strict match).
    `SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PIXTONE_IRQ_HEADROOM` strict-"0"/"1"/"2"/"3"
    resolves the inner-loop shift count (default = "1" -> shift = 9);
    only relevant when killswitch ENGAGED (DISABLED path skips the
    headroom resolve since the ISR never reads the shift). Three
    banner variants emit: ENABLED (with the headroom mode logged) /
    DISABLED / REQUESTED-but-Organya-active. Per L3 sec.5.4 + sec.6
    + flush-instr sec.24.6.

  - **DPMI locks** alongside the existing patches 0023+0025+0037+0038
    + 0069 pattern at OpenDevice: `DOS_LockCode(PixtoneISRMix,
    PixtoneISRMix_End)`, `DOS_LockData(*g_dos_pix_chan,
    sizeof(g_dos_pix_chan))`, `DOS_LockVariable(g_dos_pixtone_active
    _count)`, `DOS_LockVariable(g_dos_pixtone_irq_mix_active)`,
    `DOS_LockVariable(g_next_pix_channel_id)`,
    `DOS_LockVariable(g_dos_pixtone_irq_mix_shift)`. Per L3 sec.7.1 +
    sec.7.2 + v5 amend.

OFF-path byte-identity: when killswitch is OFF (or backend-gated off),
`SDL_DOSPixtoneStart` is never called by the engine; the ISR mix step's
`if (g_dos_pixtone_irq_mix_active)` guard fails early; the channel
pool stays zero'd; Pixtone uses SDL3_mixer unchanged. Cost: one
cached-bool read per IRQ + early branch. Sub-microsecond per IRQ.

Engine-side responsibility (nxengine-evo/0167-v2, not this patch):
  - Lock `_sound_fx[slot].raw_master_buf` at Pixtone::init (sec.7.3).
  - Route Pixtone::play through SDL_DOSPixtoneStart when Lever 3
    engaged (sec.4).
  - v1 scope: non-resampled Pixtone::play only. playResampled stays
    on SDL3_mixer for v1; v2 extension if stream SFX need IRQ-mix.

DOSBox-X smoke-gate limit per [[dosbox_not_proxy]]: DOSBox-X's DPMI
implementation does not enforce page-locking strictly; ISR-context
bugs that hard-freeze real HW often pass DOSBox-X. Lever 3 REQUIRES
real-HW DX2-66 operator iter for behavioral validation. The banner
emits at OpenDevice and the structural correctness (mix-loop correctness
on synthetic data) is testable in DOSBox-X; the actual stutter-
elimination effect + headroom calibration is real-HW-only.

Killswitch default-OFF: SDL3_mixer fallback path stays alive when off
so a real-HW DPMI-fault inside the ISR mitigates to disabled rather
than freezing. Operator can disable via the env var if any real-HW
issue surfaces; or tune the headroom env var if SFX volume calibration
is off.

LOC: v5 = v4 (456 insertions) + ~25 LOC for the headroom knob
(cached uint8 + hint parse + banner-emit math + DPMI lock). SDL
backend only; zero engine LOC. 1 new BANNERS regex entry +
SEVERITY + LABEL. BOOT.md entry per [[env_vars_document_in_user_docs]].

Workspace-local per memory/sdl_ai_policy.md; never upstreamed.

See `docs/internal/LEVER3-PIXTONE-IRQ-MIX-DESIGN.md` sec.1-7 + sec.10
(Contract lock from #117/#123 STOP-and-ack closure) + sec.10.6 (v5
mix-headroom public-header pattern) + sec.22 + sec.24.6 of
`486-CLASS-CAMPAIGN-FINDINGS.md` for the hypothesis-C verdict + Bug 6
root-cause + `DOOM-AUDIO-ARCHITECTURE-ANALYSIS.md` sec.5.3 for the
Lever 3 original spec.

